      "title": "Family in Korean",
      "title_kr": "가족",
      "body": "Korean family vocabulary is more detailed than English — it distinguishes not just the relationship, but whether you are older or younger, and whether you are male or female. For example, 'older brother' has different words depending on whether you are a boy (형) or a girl (오빠).",
      "tip": { "icon": "👨‍👩‍👧", "label": "Gender matters here", "text": "Male speakers use 형 (older brother) and 누나 (older sister). Female speakers use 오빠 (older brother) and 언니 (older sister). This is one of Korean's most distinctive features." }
